def head(title,desc):
 return '<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title>'+title+'</title><meta name="description" content="'+desc+'"><link rel="icon" href="favicon.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="public.css"><script src="public.js" defer></script></head><body>\n'

home='''<main id="main"><section class="hero" id="home"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow">A shared journey. A clearer future.</span><h1>Small contributions.<br>Shared possibilities.<br><span class="accent">That’s PoolPay.</span></h1><p>Bring your chit group together, keep every contribution in view, and make sense of each month’s progress. Less paperwork. More clarity.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="signup.html">Start with PoolPay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="how-it-works.html">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><span class="micro">New to chit funds? Our guide is open to everyone.</span></div><div class="hero-art" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative group: 20 members contributing 5,000 rupees each form a monthly pool of 1 lakh rupees over a 20-month term."><div class="orbit"></div><span class="leaf" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><div class="pool-card"><div class="card-top">TOGETHER, EACH MONTH <span class="status">Sample group</span></div><div class="pool-value">₹1,00,000</div><p>One pool. Twenty people. Shared commitment.</p><div class="avatar-row" aria-hidden="true"><span class="avatar">AK</span><span class="avatar">SR</span><span class="avatar">NP</span><span class="avatar">RM</span><span class="avatar">+16</span></div><div class="card-rule"></div><div class="card-data"><div>Per member<br><strong>₹5,000</strong></div><div>Group term<br><strong>20 months</strong></div></div></div><div class="float-note"><strong>↗ Every contribution counts.</strong>A little consistency. A collective effort.</div><span class="art-caption">Illustrative amounts, not an available plan or offer.</span></div></div></section><div class="principles"><div class="container"><b><span>01 /</span> Built around your group</b><b><span>02 /</span> Clear contribution records</b><b><span>03 /</span> Every cycle, in one place</b></div></div>
<section class="section white" id="benefits"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">An age-old idea, made easier to follow</span><h2>Individual goals.<br>A collective way forward.</h2></div><p>A chit brings people together through regular contributions. Understanding the commitment is the first step.</p></div><div class="three-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Build a saving rhythm.</h3><p>A regular contribution gives your group a shared schedule. Choose a commitment that fits your budget for the full term.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Understand your turn.</h3><p>Each cycle, a member receives the payout under the group’s agreement. In an auction chit, the accepted discount affects that amount.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Keep the picture clear.</h3><p>Know what is due, what has been recorded, and how your group is progressing. Clear records help everyone stay informed.</p></article></div><a class="text-link section-link" href="how-it-works.html">Get to know the full cycle <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="section" id="features"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Your group, more organised</span><h2>Fewer scattered records.<br>More peace of mind.</h2><p>PoolPay gives managers and members a place to keep track of the details that matter.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><span>01</span><div><h3>Set up the essentials</h3><p>Managers organise groups, members, contribution amounts and schedules.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>02</span><div><h3>Follow contributions and dues</h3><p>Record payments and review outstanding amounts without losing sight of the month.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Keep a record of each cycle</h3><p>Review auction results, payout details and your group’s progress in the dashboard.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="preview"><div class="ledger"><span class="eyebrow">A clearer monthly picture</span><h3>Your group at a glance</h3><p>Example records · Month 4 of 20</p><div class="ledger-row"><span>Monthly contribution</span><strong>₹5,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Your payment record</span><span class="tag">Recorded ✓</span></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Auction result</span><span class="tag">Available to review</span></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Group schedule</span><strong>All in one place</strong></div></div><p class="preview-caption">Illustrative preview. Your dashboard reflects your group’s records.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section white" id="how"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with the basics</span><h2>One group.<br>A repeating cycle.<br><span class="accent">Everyone plays a part.</span></h2><p>Members contribute to a common pool. A payout is allocated each cycle according to the agreement, and contributions continue until the term ends.</p><a class="text-link" href="how-it-works.html">Explore our step-by-step guide ↗</a></div><div class="calculator"><span class="eyebrow">Try a simple example</span><label for="memberCount">Number of members · one ticket each</label><select id="memberCount"><option value="10">10 members</option><option value="20" selected>20 members</option><option value="25">25 members</option></select><label for="contribution">Monthly contribution per member</label><select id="contribution"><option value="2000">₹2,000</option><option value="5000" selected>₹5,000</option><option value="10000">₹10,000</option></select><span class="micro">Gross monthly pool</span><output id="poolTotal" aria-live="polite" for="memberCount contribution">₹1,00,000</output><p class="micro" id="poolTerm">20 members × ₹5,000 · 20 monthly cycles in this example.</p><p class="micro">Before any auction discount or fees. This explains the pool size; it is not a payout or return estimate.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="faq"><div class="container faq-wrap"><div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">A little clarity goes a long way</span><h2>Good questions. Clear answers.</h2></div><details><summary>Can I learn how it works without an account?</summary><p>Yes. This homepage and the complete <a class="text-link" href="how-it-works.html">How it works guide</a> are public. You only need to log in to access your account and group records.</p></details><details><summary>Is PoolPay a chit investment plan?</summary><p>PoolPay provides tools for managing chit-group records. The examples on this website are educational, not plans you can subscribe to. Check the organiser, registration and agreement of any chit you consider.</p></details><details><summary>Do I keep paying after receiving a payout?</summary><p>Yes. Receiving your payout does not end your contribution obligation. Follow the remaining payment schedule and conditions in your chit agreement.</p></details><details><summary>How do I get started as a manager or member?</summary><p>Managers can use Sign up to create an account. Members should contact their group manager for account access and group details, then use Log in to view their records.</p></details></div></section><section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="container"><div class="cta"><div><h2>Your group’s next chapter,<br>a little more organised.</h2><p>Start managing with PoolPay, or learn the basics first.</p></div><a class="btn" href="signup.html">Create a manager account ↗</a></div></div></section></main>'''
